{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/437999-rethinking-arcanos-markings","id":437999,"title":"Rethinking Arcanos Markings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-11T21:31:32-07:00","id":437999,"title":"Rethinking Arcanos Markings","content":"I posted a few weeks ago when I realized that Flux has no Arcanos marking, asking what it might be. Then I realized that the Jade Kingdom Arcanoi and the Dark Arcanoi also lack markings, but I was helpfully pointed at some <a href=\"http://www.cattail.nu/wraithproject/archives/0305jadedark.html\" target=\"_blank\">pretty cool fan-written ones</a>. Still, nothing for Flux. Later, I started thinking to myself that my players might like a cheat-sheet of the different markings while playing, so they could reference them when I described other Wraiths to them. As I made one, I realized something: many of them are <i>lame</i>. Very few of them are consistent, or even really thematic to the Arcanos.<br /> <br /> <b>Argos = Jet Black Eyes.</b> What does that have to do with navigating the Tempest?<br /> <b>Castigate = Ink-Stained Fingers.</b> I kinda get the &quot;touched by darkness&quot; vibe, but why their fingers?<br /> <b>Embody = Dappled Skin. </b>How does that make sense?<br /> <b>Fatalism = Arcane Symbols on Face and Hands. </b>Ok, sure, that's fine.<br /> <b>Inhabit/Kinesis = Burn Marks or Circuit Patterns. </b>Why burn marks? I get the circuit patterns... if the Wraith is really into computers, but what if they prefer simpler machines?<br /> <b>Keening = Musical Instrument. </b>I <i>hate</i> the Markings that involve carrying some external item. <br /> <b>Lifeweb = Eyes Never Close.</b> This makes sense, because Lifeweb is about seeing connections. Sure.<br /> <b>Moliate = Soft Corpus <i>and/or</i> Inhuman Perfection. </b>This makes less sense, because it's <i>two different things</i> and how can you <i>see</i> soft corpus? Why are Moliate Wraiths inhumanly perfect when Wraiths can pretty much look however they want? Why can't they be ugly? They can also change their appearance easily, so I don't get the &quot;tell&quot; aspect. <br /> <b>Outrage = Oversized Muscles. </b>Makes sense.<br /> <b>Pandemonium = Black Cloak <i>and/or</i> Uncontrolled Manifestations of Weirdness.</b> The Black Cloak is annoying because, again, it's an external item rather than a &quot;marking.&quot; The incredibly broad category of &quot;uncontrolled weirdness&quot; is just too much compared to the <i>very specific</i> nature of the others.<br /> <b>Phantasm = Dramatic Bearing.</b> I'm not much for behavioral markings, either. Plus, just <i>how</i> Dramatic is Dramatic enough? This one is also way too broad.<br /> <b>Puppetry = Mannerisms from Past Hosts. </b>Same flaws as Phantasm.<br /> <b>Usury = Tally Marks on Body</b>. Makes great sense. This Wr20 trait is a far superior replacement to the old &quot;Carries Scales&quot; marking. <br /> <b>Flux = Nothing.</b> WTF?<br /> <b>Intimation = Bright Green Left Eye.</b> Why the <i>left</i> eye? Bright green eyes seems more suited to Usury, related to Greed. Intimiation is all about desires and mind control. Why green?<br /> <b>Mnemosynis = Never Blinks.</b> What has this got to do with memory? They never miss anything, maybe? <br /> <br /> So, how could the Markings be improved? Anyone have suggestions for new markings? I offer these revised markings for consideration.<br /> <br /> <b>Argos = Wind-Blown Hair &amp; Clothes</b> (the Tempest always blows around them)<br /> <b>Castigate = Jet Black Eyes</b> (they have gazed too long into the Abyss)<br /> <b>Embody = ??</b><br /> <b>Fatalism = Arcane Symbols on Face and Hands</b> (no change)<br /> <b>Inhabit/Kinesis = Grease Stained Hands</b> (more generally 'mechanical' than burns or circuits)<br /> <b>Keening = Reverberating Voice</b> (justification)<br /> <b>Lifeweb = Eyes Never Close</b> (no change)<br /> <b>Moliate = Constantly Shifting Physical Details</b> (justification)<br /> <b>Outrage = Oversized Muscles</b> (no change)<br /> <b>Pandemonium = ??</b><br /> <b>Phantasm = Sandy Footprints</b> (they're Sandmen)<br /> <b>Puppetry = Ghostly Puppet Strings Hanging from Fingers</b> (obvious)<br /> <b>Usury = Tally Marks on Body</b> (no change)<br /> <b>Flux = Mold Growing on Hair &amp; Body</b> (their powers are about decay, right?)<br /> <b>Intimation = ??</b><br /> <b>Mnemosynis = ??</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:57:26-07:00","id":438104,"title":"","content":"Deadguy's said they're already overhauling the Arcanos markings for Wr20.<br /> <br /> Looking at the previews, Argos gets both jet-black eyes and wind-blown clothing, while Inhabit gets, as the preview puts it, &quot;wear and tear mimicking that of the objects they Inhabit&quot;, Digitally inclined Artificers get circuit patterns flickering under their skin and error logs of their internal dialogues with their Shadows across their eyes. Those who go with machines or simple objects get scuff marks, gouges, seeping lubricant, or smell of exhaust and hot metal. Soulforgers get burn marks.<br /> <br /> Flux is not solely decay, it's also about strengthening and animation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T00:27:40-07:00","id":438141,"title":"","content":"Where to start... From the beginning I guess.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Argos = Jet Black Eyes.</b> What does that have to do with navigating the Tempest? </div> </div> </div>They are jet black because they are the ones who literally gaze at the Abyss, constantly and for extended periods of time. Tempest was the still Darkness and now that it is roiling with emotions and storms and odder things it's nature is still the in many ways the Abyss, it is the darkness of the Nihil. Thus extended travel through it requires a lot of gazing into it to intuit the way and stains the Argos users eyes black.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Castigate = Ink-Stained Fingers.</b> I kinda get the &quot;touched by darkness&quot; vibe, but why their fingers? </div> </div> </div>Because it is not that darkness touches them but they touch the darkness. Castigation is very hands on Arcanoi they less gaze into the Shadow and more come in touch with it and whip the evil out rather literally in fact thus the damage inflicted during Castigation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Embody = Dappled Skin. </b>How does that make sense? </div> </div> </div>This one I cannot provide with anything solid, as we never got a Guildbook for them, but I can posit my own thoughts on the matter. I believe that it symbolises how they are able to in a very real sense manifest their corpus across the shroud into the sunlit realms of flesh. So their Corpus in a way gets suntanned but as they are never truly completely able to remain there it is like a sunlight filtered through the Shroud, in this case through a shroud of leaves. So it does, at least to me, have a certain logic to it. The shroud is in a way thinner for them as htey can project themselves through it and likewise some of that light filters through onto them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fatalism = Arcane Symbols on Face and Hands. </b>Ok, sure, that's fine. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It's a pretty direct manifestation of the Arcanois nature upon the corpus of the Oracle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Inhabit/Kinesis = Burn Marks or Circuit Patterns. </b>Why burn marks? I get the circuit patterns... if the Wraith is really into computers, but what if they prefer simpler machines? </div> </div> </div>Well you forgot one type of marking here, and technically those Burn Marks are a mark of a Soulforger not Inhabit user, and that is that their Corpus is stained with oil/oily markings, which is what often happens for those who use the Ancient arts of Inhabit which were used before computers and such became a thing. This pretty clearly suggest that the Markings of Inhabit are that the users are marked by that which they possess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Keening = Musical Instrument. </b>I <i>hate</i> the Markings that involve carrying some external item. </div> </div> </div>I agree with you here but then again we never got their Guildbook either so it was never expanded. It is likely that it is just a habit of the users to carry instruments, and it tends to make using their Arcanoi easier especially since those instruments are likely Relics that give bonuses to said usage like Tools of Castigation give bonuses for Pardoners, but it is likely not the actual Markings which I would believe is most likely either hearing music constantly distracting them somewhat or being obsessed with it. Mental markings are not out of place for Arcanoi as there are already such official Markings in place so to speak and I personally happen to disagree with you on their suitability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lifeweb = Eyes Never Close.</b> This makes sense, because Lifeweb is about seeing connections. Sure. </div> </div> </div>Agreed here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Moliate = Soft Corpus <i>and/or</i> Inhuman Perfection. </b>This makes less sense, because it's <i>two different things</i> and how can you <i>see</i> soft corpus? Why are Moliate Wraiths inhumanly perfect when Wraiths can pretty much look however they want? Why can't they be ugly? They can also change their appearance easily, so I don't get the &quot;tell&quot; aspect. </div> </div> </div>Again the first is the real Marking of this Arcanoi, that is to say Soft Corpus, while the latter is something commonly associated with the users whom often use their art as beauticians or should I say the more visible users use them as such. Soft Corpus is not immediately visible, not all Arcanoi Markings are something you can just immediately spot, but it is a clear marking nevertheless as if your paying attention you will notice how their hand is softer than it should be during a handshake etc. It is a Marking not sensed through sight but touch. Considering that the Arcanoi is all about making Corpus more malleable and flowing it is rather fitting. Also it does have a visual cue if I remember correctly, too lazy to grab the Guildbook from the shelf, in that the more experienced users, remember the Markings tend to be stronger for those more advanced in the arts, have more flowing movements than other Wraiths in that in a slightly disturbing if noticed way they seem to shift their positions in way that looks like their Corpus just flows in to place instead of moving regularly. But that visual cue is just a barely noticeable side-effect, if you will, of having such Soft Corpus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Outrage = Oversized Muscles. </b>Makes sense. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pandemonium = Black Cloak <i>and/or</i> Uncontrolled Manifestations of Weirdness.</b> The Black Cloak is annoying because, again, it's an external item rather than a &quot;marking.&quot; The incredibly broad category of &quot;uncontrolled weirdness&quot; is just too much compared to the <i>very specific</i> nature of the others. </div> </div> </div>Like I told you in the previous thread about this the Cloaks are not an Arcanoi Marking but a common way for the users, Haunters specifically, to conceal the possibly physical manifestations of their <i><b>Insanities/Altered Perceptions, </b></i>which are the actual Markings of Wylding/Pandemonium, and to give them something from which to manifest their powers within the Shadowlands if need be. This, like many Markings, is best explained in the actual Guildbook but here I go again. The Wylding manifests in it's user by altering his perceptions of either distances, time or just manifesting hallucinations depending upon how the Wraith tends to use Wylding. Sometimes on some individuals these quirks, as they call them, may be more aggravated and actually manifest in their Corpus which despite there being multiple options of how, each manifestation is dependent upon the users psyche and thus likely unique, they are unmistakable as anything but manifestations of Wylding. These aggravated quirks include such examples as everything you wear on your corpus seeming to be just underneath it, that is to say basically as if you wore them under your somewhat translucent skin, that one is for someone who manifest altered perceptions of distances while another may manifest roiling storm clouds within their Corpus clearly visible for all to see (or even twisters see full page art of the Wraith in WoD:Combat by Ron Spencer to get the visual), this one is for those suffering Hallucinations, while some manifest it as after images like with the most famous example where each after image left by the Wraith is a year younger than the last until the final is around 5 or so years old, this as you probably guessed is an example of an Aggravated Quirk as manifested by someone with Altered Perceptions of Time. Really here the best thing would be for you to read the Guildbook.<br /> And yes mainly and for most this is a mental Marking, though as such it is something that can be perceived by others from the behaviour of the Haunter if he has altered perceptions of distance he may occasionally bump into things and or try to grab far away things as if they were closer, one suffering from Hallucinations may react to something that isn't there or even try to talk to something that isn't there etc., while one with altered Perceptions of Time will likely sometimes speak really fast and at others really in slow motion etc. So even wihtout an Aggravated Quirk that manifest through their Corpus it is visible even if really mental Marking.<br /> And why isn't it quite as specific as the others? Because it is about channeling energies of chaos and creation through your corpus and it is the nature of chaos, and the Wyld into which it is tied, to be unspecific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Phantasm = Dramatic Bearing.</b> I'm not much for behavioral markings, either. Plus, just <i>how</i> Dramatic is Dramatic enough? This one is also way too broad. </div> </div> </div>Again Guildbook is your friend though in this case it muddies the Marking issue somewhat by saying that it has none. The actual Marking of it are the Gossamer items and clothing worn by Sandmen, which they admit can be cast side, and the rumors that a passing of Ancient Phantasm users tend to send those close by into reverie. The Gossamer clothing itself is quite apparent as it glows slightly in the Underworld either darkly if taken from a Nightmare or brightly if taken from a Dream as well as being such that if you watch it close you can see on it's surface the dream from which it was taken moving on.<br /> So here is the first official non-Marking bearing Arcanoi. Though the Sandmen themselves have noted hat they tend to be a likeminded bunch and thus identifiable from their flair although that isn't actual proof of the Arcanoi just a way of noting that it's use commonly attracts certain kind of people.<br /> Though in addition to the Gossamer clothing no self-respecting Sandman is without a pouch or two of Sand so that is another item that can identify them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Puppetry = Mannerisms from Past Hosts. </b>Same flaws as Phantasm. </div> </div> </div>Again Guildbook is your friend. Still what it means is that they tend to carry mannerism from their previous hosts especially those they have attuned to. Speaking in mixed accents occasionally or walking in a feminine stroll even though one is male etc. It's the small things but they do add up. Also some may manifest somewhat sticky Corpus and tend to be more stuck inside their hosts as a result. Again reading the Guildbook gives you a clearer image but it doesn't change the actual Marking of course so you may still not like it. I however kinda do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Usury = Tally Marks on Body</b>. Makes great sense. This Wr20 trait is a far superior replacement to the old &quot;Carries Scales&quot; marking. </div> </div> </div>The scales are again an obvious tool, and like with previous examples likely of some aid to their Arcanoi usage, but not the actual Markings but as they never gained a Guildbook this was never more deeply explored matter until now. This is the great thing about Wraith 20th we finally get more in depth information about the Arcanoi and the Guilds that never got their own book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Flux = Nothing.</b> WTF? </div> </div> </div>Either forgotten in the original blurb in the Players Guide with the actual markings being tied to decay possibly or it actually is meant to be nothing like with Phantasm or it manifest as a behavioral quirk. Well likely see the truth once Wraith 20th rolls out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Intimation = Bright Green Left Eye.</b> Why the <i>left</i> eye? Bright green eyes seems more suited to Usury, related to Greed. Intimiation is all about desires and mind control. Why green? </div> </div> </div>TheRealDeadGuy recently teased us about this by asking did we know where it comes from but he has not yet given his answer though it could be from <a href=\"http://thegreatgatsbysandm.blogspot.fi/2011/05/green-light.html\" target=\"_blank\">Gatsby's Green Light</a> that represents, in that novel, his hopes and dreams and thus is suitable Marking for an Arcanoi that manipulates peoples desires. This could also be the reason it manifest only in one eye, aside from being more stylistic in my opinion, as it is in the novel just one light. But again we never got a Guildbook for them so no real answers here though this is one of my favourite Markings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mnemosynis = Never Blinks.</b> What has this got to do with memory? They never miss anything, maybe? </div> </div> </div>Even though they did get a Guildbook, a nice one at that, it delves no more deeply into the reaons behind this Marking though what you posited makes sense and at least I personally do not mind it being somewhat similar to that of Monitors.<br /> <br /> So in the end I wouldn't change nay of them aside from possibly taking a new look at Flux and Phantasm and seeing if they would deserve some actual markings, whether psychological or manifest, though I still like the Sandmens Gossamer which if necessary could just be expanded to mean that even if they choose not to wear any they are still somewhat touched by the Dreams and Nightmares they visit and craft and thus have some faint glow about them and their items, even if lesser than that of actual Gossamer. And the Alchemists could manifest slight marks of Decay on their Corpus, though again there is some precedence for their Markings being psychological due to them all seeming rather scientific about their Arcanoi and outlooks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:18:01-07:00","id":438891,"title":"","content":"Outrage markings doesn't really make sense to me, and it is the one I like the least (even with the Guildbook explaining it is really about spatial distortion occurring on the wraith's corpus).<br /> <br /> How we went from telekinesis and force blows to distended, oversized muscles?! The only connection I get is from the anger of the emotional outbursts Outrage powers represent and looking big and intimidating, but that is filmsy, IMO.<br /> <br /> Also, Telgar, your suggestions for Keening and Puppetry are really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:58:27-07:00","id":438935,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Spooks have to bulk up to be able to exert their strength through the Shroud? Or, to be more precise, they end up being bulked up because they are pushing through the Shroud all the time. <br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of internalized, behavioral Arcanoi markings. The universe loves to doodle on wraiths. Vide Deathmarks. Those aren't subtle internalized character ticks or perceptually based. So why should the Guildmarks be any different? Deathmarks are the physical manifestation of what happened when a living soul becomes a wraith. Arcanoi marking are what happens afterwards. Also, since there is manifest danger in developing Arcanoi markings for many of the Guilds whose sole purpose was breaking the Dictum Mortuum, it gives an edge to the Guilds whose marks are just &quot;he might be acting a little hinky&quot; in a setting where EVERYONE is acting hinky ALL THE TIM, what with he internal dialogue with their Shadows and the push and pull of their Passions and Fetters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}